  "limitations": [
    "Gross retaliation can be fully restored later in the same roll; it is not the same as net lost HP.",
    "This fixed self-selected policy and its small losses still do not establish general survival pressure or human win rates.",
    "Each branch is free; no conclusion about paid upgrade value follows. Lower max HP can clip current HP immediately; swapHpLoss is separate from battle damage.",
    "Continuation retains the selected loadout, invests new points in power, claims rewards and uses free rest; it declines events and further paid services.",
    "The first battle may already be partly played. A window counts twelve completed combat attempts, or the first death. Later RNG, loot, leveling and healing may diverge because of legal choices.",
    "Raw report preserves full generated audit output. First-hit individual roll sequences are retained as trace hashes and are regenerated by the replay script, not individually embedded in this report.",
    "A natural single-roll sign difference is not an estimator error rate.",
    "No general optimal-equipment, human win-rate, or paid-upgrade-value conclusion follows.",
    "Cross-version all-state fingerprint equality normalizes only runId to date-normalized, and gameplayOnly excludes detail/hint/adapter plus outer version metadata. It is not raw full-report or raw state byte equality; the fourteen per-version encode/decode deep-equality assertions use no normalization."
  ],
